module

public import CFSG.Quasithin.ChapterB.Section01.FittingStructure.GlobalSplitting.BestOffenderSplitting.Basic
public import CFSG.Quasithin.ChapterB.Section01.FittingStructure.GlobalSplitting.BestOffenderSplitting.Normalization
public import CFSG.Quasithin.ChapterB.Section01.FittingStructure.GlobalSplitting.BestOffenderSplitting.CentralizerProjection

/-!
# Best offenders and the Fitting centralizer

Write E for the subgroup generated by the actual source S₃ groups Gᵢ and
R=J_P(C_G(F)) for the subgroup generated by the best offenders centralizing
F=[F(G),J*]. We prove J(G,V)=E⊔R; the re-exported centralizer result gives
R≤C_G(E), and E and R have trivial intersection.

Every best offender normalizes each Gᵢ by the solvable local action argument
in Normalization. CentralizerProjection then projects it to a trivial subgroup
or a best offender of the original representation in C_G(E)≤C_G(F).
Thus every generating best offender lies in E⊔R. Both E and R already lie in
J(G,V), giving equality without an extra normalization or projection premise.

Nontriviality of F is unnecessary for these subgroup relations. The local-plane
law remains the explicit task input. The parent GlobalSplitting module owns
the inclusion-compatible groupProduct and the final B.1.9 assembly.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, B.1.9(1), printed p.71 (PDF p.82).
-/

public section

open Subgroup Representation.BinaryOffender
namespace CFSG.Quasithin.ChapterB.FittingStructure

variable {G V : Type*} [Group G] [Finite G] [AddCommGroup V] [Module (ZMod 2) V]
  [FiniteDimensional (ZMod 2) V] (ρ : Representation (ZMod 2) G V)

/-- The subgroup equality in B.1.9(1), with the literal source factors and
the best offenders of the original representation in the F-centralizer.
The normalization premise of the projection theorem is fully discharged. -/
theorem offenderSubgroup_eq_planeGenerated_sup_centralizingBestGenerated
    (hρ : Function.Injective ρ) (hcore : pCore 2 G = ⊥) (hlocal : LocalPlaneLaw ρ) :
    offenderSubgroup ρ = planeGenerated ρ ⊔ centralizingBestGenerated ρ := by
  apply le_antisymm
  · exact offenderSubgroup_le_planeGenerated_sup_centralizingBestGenerated ρ hρ hlocal
      (fun _ hB i =>
        BestOffenderNormalization.best_normalizes_cubic_plane ρ hρ hcore hlocal hB i)
  · exact sup_le (planeGenerated_le_offenderSubgroup ρ)
      (centralizingBestGenerated_le_offenderSubgroup ρ)

end CFSG.Quasithin.ChapterB.FittingStructure
